.TP
.B Type Safety
All methods use PHP 8.1+ type declarations with union types where appropriate
.TP
.B Nullable Returns
Many getter methods return nullable types to handle cases where information is not available
.TP
.B Default Parameters
Most optional parameters have sensible defaults matching PROJ library behavior
.TP
.B Array Handling
Methods accept both single values and arrays for batch operations
.TP
.B Direction Handling
ProjTransformer uses string direction parameter (FORWARD/INVERSE/IDENT), while Proj class uses boolean $inverse parameter for backward compatibility
.TP
.B Coordinate Order
Default behavior respects CRS axis order unless $always_xy is set to true
.TP
.B Error Handling
All operations throw specific exception types for different error conditions

.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B PROJ Library
>= 6.0.0 (detected via pkg-config)
.TP
.B PHP
8.1+ (uses modern arginfo declarations)
.TP
.B Build Tools
phpize, autotools, pkg-config

